# ============================================================
# Hay Straw Length Measurement Workflow
# ============================================================
# MODES:
#   1. HSV Mode   — classic color segmentation (no model needed)
#   2. YOLO Mode  — YOLOv11 instance segmentation (uses best.pt)
#
# YOLO INTEGRATION:
#   This script uses your trained instance segmentation model.
#   Each straw detection comes with its own pixel-level mask,
#   which is fed directly into skeletonization and length
#   measurement. No HSV color segmentation needed per straw.
#
#   In YOLO mode, debug popup windows are suppressed. The final
#   overlay image for each processed image is saved to disk AND
#   embedded as a photo in the Excel results file.
#
# CALIBRATION:
#   When CALIBRATION_MODE = "auto", the pipeline looks for a YOLO
#   detection whose class name matches QUARTER_CLASS_NAME.
#   - Fits an ellipse to the quarter mask if available (most accurate)
#   - Falls back to bounding-box (w+h)/2 if no mask
#   A US quarter is 24.26 mm in diameter, so:
#       pixel_to_mm = QUARTER_DIAMETER_MM / pixel_diameter
#
#   CALIBRATION_PER_IMAGE = True  -> recalibrate from each image
#   CALIBRATION_PER_IMAGE = False -> calibrate once from first image
#                                    that contains a quarter; reuse for rest
#
# OVERLAP SEPARATION:
#   When straws cross, their skeletons merge at a branch point,
#   producing 4+ endpoints instead of 2. This script:
#     1. Finds all skeleton endpoints in an overlap region
#     2. Computes the angle each endpoint points away from the crossing
#     3. Clusters endpoints that are angularly opposite (~180 apart)
#        and within a spatial proximity radius
#     4. Pairs them as belonging to the same straw piece
#     5. Traces the Dijkstra path between each valid pair
#   This reconstructs individual straw lengths through crossings.
# ============================================================

